━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ RuleCells is Tuple

` The locals a rule a part calls writes: where it stopped, how far it read and where it failed.

+ ended LocalId
+ reached LocalId
+ erred LocalId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Lending is Tuple

` A list of the caller's a call lends a function, as a collector in memory of the frame:
` that memory, and the list among the lists of captures.

+ memory Operand
+ level U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ LevelMark is Tuple

` How many items a list held where a part of a pattern began, which it is cut back to where
` the part fails: the list among the lists of captures, and the local that holds the count.

+ level U32
+ mark LocalId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ArmGroup is Tuple

` Alternatives of a choice that may start with the same items, as the reference groups them:
` their places, in order, and the ranges of the items any of them may start with.

+ arms [U32]
+ ranges [ItemRange]

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ArmWay is Tuple

` How the alternatives of a choice are emitted: as the arms of a match or a rule, which join
` with the value each gives, of the type `result`, after reading the whole input where
` `whole`, and keep where each ended in `end`; or as `parts` of a pattern, which join with
` where each ended, and where the choice gives a value leave theirs, of the type `result`, in
` `end`. `site` is the choice. `unread` says nothing reads the value arms join with.

+ site SyntaxId
+ result TypeId
+ whole Bool
+ end LocalId
+ joined IRBlockId
+ slot Operand
+ parts Bool
+ unread Bool

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ RuleTarget is Tuple

` The pattern of a rule a call names, the module whose syntax it is, and the instance whose
` facts and binding are read for it.

+ module ModuleId
+ owner InstanceId
+ pattern SyntaxId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Streams is facet of FunctionEmitter
    sees Cleanups
    sees Loops
    sees MatchArms
    sees Tables

_ scanning = false
_ first-cuts U64 = 0
_ deferred-part U64 = U64.max
_ adapting FunctionId = no-function

────────────────────
_ do pattern-value Typed
    - arg SyntaxId

` A pattern given to a rule, as the value of the function type the rule's parameter takes:
` the function made of it, or the one that runs the rule it calls alone, with no data. One
` made of a pattern that is given what names hold has as its data the address of memory of
` the frame that holds them, each read here as it is where the pattern is passed.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. helper = tables.pattern-argument-of(unit.reading, arg)
. type = facts.node-type(unit.reading, arg)
. layout = layout-of(type, arg)
if helper == no-function || layout != tables.layouts.function-layout
    refuse(.refused-expression, arg)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. target = tables.functions[helper]
. row = facts.pattern-arguments[target.place]
. data = integer(.machine-pointer, 0)
if target.kind == .pattern-helper && row.params.count != 0
    . held = tables.pattern-environment(target.place)
    if held == no-layout
        refuse(.refused-expression, arg)
        = Typed(nothing, no-type)
    . memory = frame(held)
    zero(memory, held)
    for offset in 0 .. < row.params.count
        . position = row.params.start + offset
        . value = slot-value(facts.action-slots[position], arg, facts.action-types[position])
        put(memory, tables.layouts.field(held, offset), value.operand, arg)
    data = address(memory, 0, pointer-layout, arg)
ir.depend(.callee-function, helper, if target.may-panic then may-panic-dependency else 0u32)
. made = frame(layout)
store(made, 0, make-operand(.operand-symbol, target.symbol), false, arg)
store(made, tables.layouts.field(layout, 1).offset, data, false, arg)
= Typed(made, type)

────────────────────
_ do rule-argument Operand
    - position U32
    - id SyntaxId

` An argument the rule being emitted was given, for the function of one of its local rules:
` the argument, or in the function made of a pattern, what the function was given for it.
if !given-slots
    = make-operand(.operand-argument, position)
for offset in 0 .. < unit.slot-count
    . slot = unit.slot-start + offset
    if bindings.slots[slot].kind == .slot-argument && owns(slot) && bound-here
        = read-bound(slot, id, instances.argument-type(unit.instance, position)).operand
    .. bound-here = unit.positions[offset] == position && is-bound(slot)
refuse(.refused-expression, id)
= make-operand(.operand-void, 0)

────────────────────
+ do emit-stream-match Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - subject SyntaxId
    - matched SyntaxId
    - helper SyntaxId
    - is-statement Bool

` A grammar run on the value a match is on, as `run-stream-match` runs it, with the
` helper of an enclosing match set aside while it runs.
. own-streaming = streaming
streaming = streaming.pattern-helper-type = no-type
. answer = run-stream-match(id, subject, matched, helper, is-statement)
streaming = own-streaming
= answer

────────────────────
_ do run-stream-match Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - subject SyntaxId
    - matched SyntaxId
    - helper SyntaxId
    - is-statement Bool

` A grammar run on the value a match is on, as the reference runs one. The value is read into
` the stream the type pass chose for it, whose `pattern-view` gives the buffer, where the pattern
` starts and how many items the buffer holds, through the calls the type pass recorded at the
` pattern, in order. The arms are tried in turn from the start, and the first that passes gives the
` match its value: no arm after it is tried. An arm passes only where its pattern read the whole
` input, but on a stream the match is given, which it reads only as far as an arm matches. Such a
` stream, and one made of the value that pulls its items as they are needed, may give more input as
` it is read: each part that reads past the end of its buffer asks it for more and goes on with what
` it gives. The stream then commits where the pattern ended, or where it started, and how far it
` read. A match whose last arm can fail is optional, and holds nothing where no arm passed. One
` whose last arm raises panics. The match `if` or `while` tests a pattern with gives what its arm
` gives, and false where no arm passed. Each name the pattern captures has its place while the arms
` are emitted. A helper the type pass planned is kept for the values it makes. A match on a String
` or an array makes its stream inside an allocation scope of the task's parse region, as
` TypeScript routes that stream, and gives the region back to where it stood once the match
` ends.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. type = facts.node-type(unit.reading, matched)
. pattern SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[matched]
    | .node-stream-match(row)
        pattern = row.pattern
if pattern == 0 || type == no-type || type == invalid-type || mistyped
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
.. mistyped = !is-statement && facts.node-type(unit.reading, id) != type
. always = stream-always-passes(pattern)
. opens = facts.plan-of(unit.reading, matched) == .plan-open
. result = facts.node-type(unit.reading, pattern)
if result == no-type
    refuse(.refused-expression, matched)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. layout = if is-statement then void-layout else layout-of(type, id)
. value = emit-expression(subject)
. subject-type = value.type
if helper != 0
    . kept = emit-expression(helper)
    if facts.plan-of(unit.reading, helper) == .plan-pattern-helper
        streaming = streaming.pattern-helper = kept.operand
        streaming = streaming.pattern-helper-type = kept.type
. first = facts.first-call(unit.reading, matched)
. made = stream-maker(matched)
. viewed = if made != no-fact then next-call(made) else first
. commits = next-call(viewed)
. extends = next-call(commits)
if commits == no-fact
    refuse(.refused-expression, matched)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. named = bound.length
. subject-slot = arm-slot-of(id, .slot-it)
if subject-slot != no-slot
    bound += BoundValue(subject-slot, subject-type, value.operand)
. regional = subject-type == types.string-type || array-subject
    .. array-subject = same-decl(class-ref(types, subject-type), types.array-decl)
. region-mark = if regional then make-operand(.operand-value, append(.op-load-task-word, matched, Span(), parse-region-mark-offset, u64-layout)) else nothing
. run = open-stream(matched, value.operand, subject-type, made, viewed, extends, regional)
. done = ir.reserve-block()
. slot = if is-statement then nothing else join-slot(layout)
. mark = joins.length
. failed = ir.reserve-block()
. given = attempt-arms(matched, pattern, result, run, made != no-fact, commits, failed, false)
if is-statement
    jump(done)
else if always || opens
    arrive(matched, given.operand, done, slot)
else
    arrive(matched, wrap(matched, Typed(given.operand, result), type).operand, done, slot)
ir.start-block(failed)
if opens && !is-statement
    arrive(matched, integer(.machine-u8, 0), done, slot)
else if always
    raise-text(matched, "Grammar match failed")
else if is-statement
    jump(done)
else
    arrive(matched, empty-optional(type, layout).operand, done, slot)
drop-bound(named)
if is-statement
    ir.start-block(done)
    reset-region(regional, region-mark, matched)
    = Typed(nothing, types.void-type)
. answer = close-joins(done, mark, layout, slot)
reset-region(regional, region-mark, matched)
= Typed(answer, type)

────────────────────
_ do reset-region
    - regional Bool
    - mark Operand
    - site SyntaxId

` Gives the task's parse region back to where it stood at a mark, where a match made its stream
` there.
if !regional
    =
. start = pending.length
pending += mark
call-runtime(.runtime-parse-region-reset, site, start)

────────────────────
+ do emit-scoped-match Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - pattern SyntaxId

` A grammar written in the code of a function declared over the items of a stream, run
` on the stream the function is given as `attempt-arms` runs one on a stream a match is
` given: from where the stream stands, only as far as an arm matches, asking the stream for
` more where a part reads past the end of its buffer. Where an arm passed it gives a
` `CaptureResult` of the items the pattern read, as an array that shares the buffer's, and of
` what the arm gave; where none did, nothing. In the code of a local rule, as `coded-call`
` runs it, the stream is the one the rule was called on. The helper of an enclosing match is
` set aside while it runs. A result it gives is counted where the type pass marked the pattern
` for the profile.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. type = facts.node-type(unit.reading, id)
. result = facts.node-type(unit.reading, pattern)
. given-slot = no-slot
for offset in 0 .. < unit.slot-count
    if bindings.slots[unit.slot-start + offset].kind == .slot-argument && unit.positions[offset] == 0
        given-slot = unit.slot-start + offset
. coded-in = streaming.given-stream-type != no-type
if subjectless || result == no-type || not-optional
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
.. subjectless = !coded-in && (unit.reading != unit.instance || given-slot == no-slot)
.. not-optional = type == no-type || type == invalid-type || !types.is-optional(type)
. captured = types.optional-inner(type)
. layout = layout-of(type, id)
. captured-layout = layout-of(captured, id)
. viewed = facts.first-call(unit.reading, id)
. commits = next-call(viewed)
. extends = next-call(commits)
. counted = next-call(extends)
. counts = counted != no-fact && probe-metric && next-call(counted) == no-fact
    .. probe-metric = facts.calls[counted].form == .call-probe-metric
if commits == no-fact || (counted != no-fact && !counts) || not-capture-result
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
.. not-capture-result = !same-decl(class-ref(types, captured), types.capture-result-decl)
if !tables.layouts.is-struct(captured-layout) || unpaired-capture
    refuse(.refused-type, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
.. unpaired-capture = tables.layouts.rows[captured-layout].fields.count != 2
. subject-type = if coded-in then streaming.given-stream-type else instances.argument-type(unit.instance, 0)
. subject = if coded-in then streaming.given-stream else slot-value(given-slot, id, subject-type).operand
. own-streaming = streaming
streaming = streaming.pattern-helper-type = no-type
streaming = streaming.given-stream-type = no-type
. run = open-stream(id, subject, subject-type, no-fact, viewed, extends)
. done = ir.reserve-block()
. slot = join-slot(layout)
. mark = joins.length
. failed = ir.reserve-block()
. given = attempt-arms(id, pattern, result, run, false, commits, failed, false)
streaming = own-streaming
. items-field = tables.layouts.field(captured-layout, 0)
. result-field = tables.layouts.field(captured-layout, 1)
if other-buffer || result-field.layout != layout-of(result, id)
    refuse(.refused-type, id)
.. other-buffer = items-field.layout != run.buffer-layout
. number = if counts then tables.probe-number(unit.reading, id) else 0
if number != 0
    . start = pending.length
    pending += integer(.machine-u16, number)
    pending += integer(.machine-u64, 1)
    call-runtime(.runtime-profile-counter-add, id, start)
. items = stream-slice(run, id, run.start, load-local(attempt-end, id))
. made = frame(captured-layout)
put(made, items-field, items.operand, id)
put(made, result-field, given.operand, id)
arrive(id, wrap(id, Typed(made, captured), type).operand, done, slot)
ir.start-block(failed)
arrive(id, empty-optional(type, layout).operand, done, slot)
. answer = close-joins(done, mark, layout, slot)
= Typed(answer, type)

────────────────────
+ do attempt-arms Typed
    - site SyntaxId
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - result TypeId
    - run StreamRun
    - whole Bool
    - commits FactId
    - failure IRBlockId
    - keeps Bool

` The arms of a grammar tried on the view of a stream, from where it starts, as the
` reference tries them: where the input must be read `whole`, an arm passes only where it
` read the whole of it. A stream that may give more input is asked for it where a part reads
` past the end of its buffer, and the part goes on from there. Where an arm passes, the stream
` commits where it ended and how far the pattern read, and what the arm gives is given, with
` `attempt-end` left the local that keeps where it ended; where none does, the stream commits
` where the pattern started, and goes on to `failure`. How far the pattern read is kept no
` farther than the end of the input, as `settle-extent` says. The names the pattern captures
` are bound while the arms are emitted, and after them where the pattern `keeps` them. A
` pattern the type pass found holds a rollback mark gives back the one it holds where it
` fails, as the reference does; the marks of a pattern it runs in are set aside while it is
` emitted.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. arm-layout = layout-of(result, site)
. own-streaming = streaming
open-marks(site)
streaming = streaming.storage-row = facts.storage-body-of(unit.reading, site)
streaming = streaming.observer-row = facts.observer-body-of(unit.reading, site)
. end = ir.add-local(run.index-layout)
. arms-joined = ir.reserve-block()
. failed = ir.reserve-block()
. arm-slot = join-slot(arm-layout)
. arms-mark = joins.length
. held = bound.length
. captured = stream-captures.length
. arrives = false
if adapting != no-function
    arrives = adapt-arms(run, site, result, end, arms-joined, arm-slot, failed)
else
    hold-captures(run, pattern)
    plan-choices(pattern)
    arrives = emit-stream-arms(run, pattern, result, run.start, whole, end, arms-joined, arm-slot, failed)
if !keeps || !arrives
    drop-bound(held)
    drop-captures(captured)
if !arrives
    refuse(.refused-expression, site)
    drop-joins(arms-mark)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. given = close-joins(arms-joined, arms-mark, arm-layout, arm-slot)
settle-extent(run, site)
commit-stream(run, commits, load-local(end, site))
. passing = ir.reserve-block()
jump(passing)
ir.start-block(failed)
rewind-mark(site)
settle-extent(run, site)
commit-stream(run, commits, run.start)
jump(failure)
ir.start-block(passing)
streaming = own-streaming
attempt-end = end
= Typed(given, result)

────────────────────
_ do open-stream StreamRun
    - site SyntaxId
    - subject Operand
    - subject-type TypeId
    - made FactId
    - viewed FactId
    - extends FactId
    - regional Bool = false

` The stream a pattern reads the value a match is on through, and the view of it the pattern
` runs over. A value that is a stream, and a `ChunkedTokenStream` made of the value, may give
` more input as it is read. A `regional` stream is made inside an allocation scope of the task's
` parse region.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. closed = StreamRun
    - site
    - nothing
    - no-type
    - nothing
    - no-type
    - nothing
    - nothing
    - nothing
    - no-local
    - no-local
    - void-layout
    - void-layout
    - void-layout
if regional
    . begin = tree.nodes[site].loc.begin
    . start = pending.length
    pending += integer(.machine-u64, begin.line + 1)
    pending += integer(.machine-u64, begin.column + 1)
    call-runtime(.runtime-parse-region-enter-scope, site, start)
. stream = stream-of(site, subject, subject-type, made)
. stream-type = stream.type
if regional
    call-runtime(.runtime-parse-region-leave-scope, site, pending.length)
. refills = made == no-fact || chunked
    .. chunked = same-decl(class-ref(types, stream-type), types.chunked-token-stream-decl)
= view-stream(site, stream.operand, stream-type, refills, viewed, extends)

────────────────────
+ do stream-of Typed
    - site SyntaxId
    - subject Operand
    - subject-type TypeId
    - made FactId

` The stream a pattern reads a value through, by the calls the type pass recorded for it: a
` value that is a stream converted to the `TokenStream` it is, and any other value, a String
` among them, given to the stream the type pass chose.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
if made == no-fact
    . stream = convert(site, .reason-argument, Typed(subject, subject-type))
    if types.intrinsic-of(stream.type) != .interface
        refuse(.refused-conversion, site)
        = Typed(nothing, no-type)
    = stream
= make-stream(site, made, subject, subject-type)

────────────────────
+ do view-stream StreamRun
    - site SyntaxId
    - stream Operand
    - stream-type TypeId
    - refills Bool
    - viewed FactId
    - extends FactId

` The view of a stream a pattern runs over, as its `pattern-view` gives it: the buffer, where
` the pattern starts and how many items the buffer holds, read as it lies, or as its
` `pattern-text-view` gives the UTF-8 bytes of a String's characters. How far the pattern
` reads, and the farthest cursor a part of it fails at, are kept from the start. A stream that
` `refills` may give more input as it is read: the buffer, where its items start and how many
` it holds are kept, to be read again where its `pattern-extend` gives more.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. closed = StreamRun
    - site
    - nothing
    - no-type
    - nothing
    - no-type
    - nothing
    - nothing
    - nothing
    - no-local
    - no-local
    - void-layout
    - void-layout
    - void-layout
. view = call-protocol(site, viewed, stream, stream-type, nothing)
if !types.is-optional(view.type)
    refuse(.refused-type, site)
    = closed
. held = payload(site, view)
. tuple-layout = layout-of(held.type, site)
. buffer = part(held.operand, tuple-layout, 0, site)
. buffer-type = buffer.type
. start = part(held.operand, tuple-layout, 1, site)
. start-type = start.type
. length = part(held.operand, tuple-layout, 2, site)
. length-type = length.type
. buffer-layout = layout-of(buffer-type, site)
. index-layout = layout-of(types.index-type, site)
. size-layout = layout-of(types.size-type, site)
. item-layout = layout-of(class-arg(types, buffer-type, 0), site)
if start-type != types.index-type || length-type != types.size-type
    refuse(.refused-type, site)
    = closed
if !tables.layouts.is-struct(buffer-layout) || unpaired-buffer || !is-integer(index-layout)
    refuse(.refused-type, site)
    = closed
.. unpaired-buffer = tables.layouts.rows[buffer-layout].fields.count != 2
. data = part(buffer.operand, buffer-layout, 0, site)
. data-layout = layout-of(data.type, site)
if !is-pointer(data-layout)
    refuse(.refused-type, site)
    = closed
. extent = ir.add-local(index-layout)
store-local(extent, start.operand, site)
. error = ir.add-local(index-layout)
store-local(error, start.operand, site)
. length-index = num-cast(site, length.operand, size-layout, index-layout)
. run = StreamRun
    - site
    - stream
    - stream-type
    - buffer.operand
    - buffer-type
    - num-cast(site, data.operand, data-layout, pointer-layout)
    - start.operand
    - length-index
    - extent
    - error
    - index-layout
    - item-layout
    - buffer-layout
    - viewed
    - extends
if !refills
    = run
if extends == no-fact
    refuse(.refused-type, site)
    = closed
. kept-buffer = ir.add-local(buffer-layout)
store-local(kept-buffer, buffer.operand, site)
. kept-data = ir.add-local(pointer-layout)
store-local(kept-data, run.data, site)
. kept-length = ir.add-local(index-layout)
store-local(kept-length, length-index, site)
= StreamRun
    - site
    - stream
    - stream-type
    - buffer.operand
    - buffer-type
    - run.data
    - start.operand
    - length-index
    - extent
    - error
    - index-layout
    - item-layout
    - buffer-layout
    - viewed
    - extends
    - kept-buffer
    - kept-data
    - kept-length

────────────────────
_ do make-stream Typed
    - site SyntaxId
    - made FactId
    - given Operand
    - given-type TypeId

` The stream the type pass chose to read a value through, made of it: given the value,
` converted as the type pass recorded, then the defaults its other parameters take.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
if facts.calls[made].form != .call-constructor || !is-callable(facts.calls[made].callee)
    refuse(.refused-expression, site)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. maker = facts.calls[made].callee
. signature = instances.signatures[maker]
. count = signature.args.count
if count == 0 || count > 2 || signature.errors.count != 0
    refuse(.refused-expression, site)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. parameter = instances.argument-type(maker, 0)
. value = given
if given-type != parameter
    . converted = convert(site, .reason-argument, Typed(given, given-type))
    value = converted.operand
    if converted.type != parameter
        refuse(.refused-conversion, site)
        = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. mark = pending.length
pending += value
if count == 2
    . default = parameter-default(maker, 1)
    if default == 0
        refuse(.refused-expression, site)
        drop-pending(mark)
        = Typed(nothing, no-type)
    pending += default-argument(site, maker, default, instances.argument-type(maker, 1)).operand
= call-instance(maker, site, mark)

────────────────────
_ do run-buffer Operand
    - run StreamRun
    - site SyntaxId

` The buffer of the stream's view as the pattern last read it, or in a rule's function, which
` is given where the items start and their count, an array that shares them.
if run.kept-buffer != no-local
    = load-local(run.kept-buffer, site)
if operand-kind(run.buffer) == .operand-void
